WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:03.940
<b>Kabukicho Ichibangai</b>

00:06.440 --> 00:08.940
Fortunes

00:09.950 --> 00:12.150
Think I filled out this questionnaire okay?

00:12.150 --> 00:13.240
Looks good to me!

00:13.240 --> 00:15.330
Hey, is this place legit?

00:15.330 --> 00:16.370
Absolutely.

00:16.370 --> 00:18.580
You mean it?!

00:18.580 --> 00:19.450
Yes.

00:19.670 --> 00:23.160
This is my second visit,
but I was sure by the end of my first time.

00:23.420 --> 00:26.130
This fortune teller is the real deal!

00:26.130 --> 00:30.590
He even knew I hurt my leg,
and only my coworkers know that!

00:30.590 --> 00:31.780
Wow!

00:31.780 --> 00:33.720
I can't wait!

00:35.720 --> 00:37.650
So, have you found out anything?

00:37.650 --> 00:42.810
I spent all night looking into 
that symbol, but no dice.

00:43.030 --> 00:47.770
I think it was part of a serious case, 
though. Public Safety got involved.

00:47.770 --> 00:53.210
And Inspector Hosorogi went 
missing while tracking it down.

00:54.240 --> 00:58.070
Well, that's mostly correct. 
They got me right before I got them. 
You know the rest.

01:00.280 --> 01:04.790
The ones who killed me in this building 
were most likely hired assassins,

01:01.430 --> 01:04.790
not the enemy I was chasing themselves.

01:04.790 --> 01:06.290
You mean...?

01:06.290 --> 01:12.080
If an IA inspector was on the case, 
the culprit must have been a cop.

01:13.630 --> 01:16.880
I'm sorry. I can't speak of the culprit without
definitive proof. It would get you involved.

01:16.880 --> 01:20.250
Oh, I'd say we're plenty involved already.

01:20.250 --> 01:22.350
I'll be fine,

01:22.660 --> 01:26.380
but what about Polka-kun and the Shinoyamas?

01:27.770 --> 01:30.720
Yes, I'm worried about them.

01:31.270 --> 01:35.030
Exactly. That's why I asked you to tread carefully.

01:36.410 --> 01:39.720
<i>So, this Hosorogi person </i>is<i> involved.</i>

01:39.720 --> 01:41.660
<i>But corruption in the police?</i>

01:41.920 --> 01:45.910
<i>What the hell are these 
crooks trying to fight?</i>

01:45.910 --> 01:48.450
Xiaoyu-kun, I'm starving.

01:48.450 --> 01:50.410
I'll be right there!

01:50.410 --> 01:53.770
<i>Still, there are strange 
pauses in their conversation.</i>

01:53.770 --> 01:56.650
<i>And do I hear a mechanical pencil again?</i>

01:58.820 --> 02:00.470
I was able to give my message to the right person.

02:00.860 --> 02:03.210
You mean that detective? Iwanome?

02:04.560 --> 02:06.350
Although this is one of my regrets...

02:11.960 --> 02:15.990
I want... to entrust it to him.
We pursued this case together.

03:48.730 --> 03:52.730
As you can see, Solitaire is elusive.

03:50.200 --> 03:54.170
<b>Special Investigation Team
All Ten'a Sorimura Cases</b>

03:53.160 --> 03:58.130
While I realize an investigator 
shouldn't use that word lightly,

03:58.130 --> 04:03.840
<b><i>Ten'a Sorimura
self-professed
magician</i></b>

03:58.130 --> 04:03.840
<b><i>Youji Iwazono
(46)
Yougan-gumi
Leader</i></b>

03:58.130 --> 04:03.840
<b><i>The Poisoner
(60–70~)</i></b>

03:58.360 --> 04:03.840
I hope you understand that, 
in his case, I have no choice.

04:04.640 --> 04:08.800
However, the suspect has a tendency 
to move in for a closer look

04:08.800 --> 04:10.950
at anything that catches his interest.

04:12.550 --> 04:13.390
In other words,

04:13.850 --> 04:19.110
if we follow this symbol Solitaire is after,
we're likely to cross paths.

04:19.110 --> 04:21.710
What're these Shinjuku cops doing here?

04:19.770 --> 04:22.910
You'll find the details 
on page 12 of my report.

04:21.710 --> 04:26.910
Even Arase and Pop Tozawa.
It's like a loose cannon convention.

04:23.990 --> 04:29.590
Solitaire likes to show off and 
attracts public attention by doing so,

04:29.590 --> 04:32.780
After the shit he stirred 
up with that IA inspector,

04:30.090 --> 04:32.750
but he also excels at disguise.

04:32.780 --> 04:36.500
who does he think he is to lecture us?

04:33.370 --> 04:36.500
He currently uses at least three 
identities that we know of, and...

04:36.520 --> 04:39.960
<b>Fortunes</b>

04:36.520 --> 04:39.960
<b>Reception desk opens at 10:00 a.m.</b>

04:36.520 --> 04:39.960
<b>Please fill out the questionnaire
you receive with...</b>

04:37.690 --> 04:39.480
Shouta Yamanoura-san,

04:39.960 --> 04:43.860
you are standing at a crossroads 
of great significance,

04:43.860 --> 04:46.390
or so I read in the currents.

04:46.820 --> 04:52.100
Your ship is about to founder on 
unseen rocks steeped in ostentation.

04:52.100 --> 04:53.100
What?!

04:53.100 --> 04:57.560
Before it sinks, you should 
seek another vessel to board.

04:57.770 --> 05:02.080
I... I didn't mention anything 
about that in my survey,

05:02.660 --> 05:04.670
but you got everything right.

05:05.030 --> 05:09.930
<i>If I really were Shouta 
Yamanoura-kun, that is!</i>

05:09.640 --> 05:13.180
<b>Exclusive Exposé!


Three Secrets of the Office Worker!</b>

05:10.100 --> 05:13.180
<b>1) He's actually
Solitaire!</b>

05:10.390 --> 05:13.180
<b>2) He uses Hollywood special effects makeup (self-taught)!</b>

05:10.800 --> 05:13.180
<b>3) The real
Yamanoura
is a normal
guy who has
nothing to do 
with Solitaire!</b>

05:11.810 --> 05:13.180
<b>The   End</b>

05:12.070 --> 05:14.870
<i>But he did all that using hot reading,</i>

05:15.150 --> 05:20.820
<i>probably courtesy of that hacker 
Nanny mentioned, Takumi Kuruya.</i>

05:21.130 --> 05:25.520
<i>Yamanoura's company cooking the 
books hasn't made the news.</i>

05:25.520 --> 05:29.000
<i>Finding out about it in such 
a short time is impressive...</i>

05:29.000 --> 05:31.680
<i>but unfortunately, I suppose,</i>

05:32.180 --> 05:35.230
<i>this fortune teller is a mere mortal.</i>

05:36.600 --> 05:39.060
Huh? Was something I said that shocking?

05:39.560 --> 05:40.820
Oh, well.

05:40.820 --> 05:42.840
Now, um...

05:42.840 --> 05:45.250
Do you have any questions for me?

05:45.250 --> 05:49.780
Questions? Well, let me see...

05:50.030 --> 05:51.580
You know that symbol?

05:51.580 --> 05:56.000
The one Solitaire offered 
300 million yen for figuring out?

05:56.250 --> 06:00.370
Do you think you could 
see what it really is?

06:01.410 --> 06:04.710
Ah. I'm afraid that is beyond even my sight.

06:05.040 --> 06:08.220
<i>Well, no surprise there.</i>

06:10.180 --> 06:11.090
However,

06:12.120 --> 06:14.720
I sense something not quite 
right about that symbol.

06:15.090 --> 06:16.240
Not quite right?

06:16.900 --> 06:19.360
As if something unnecessary 
has been added to it.

06:20.270 --> 06:24.220
And drawing on the power of fate, 
which makes the world go round,

06:24.600 --> 06:26.690
I will now reveal it.

06:28.720 --> 06:31.640
<i>Well, now, this is something.</i>

06:31.640 --> 06:35.370
<i>The writing's too firm for it to be 
wires or magnetism.</i>

06:35.720 --> 06:36.690
<i>Hmm...</i>

06:36.690 --> 06:40.060
<i>His magic tricks are more 
interesting than his fortune—</i>

06:41.710 --> 06:45.680
The proper symbol has one 
less horizontal line.

06:45.680 --> 06:47.020
So I have seen.

06:50.510 --> 06:52.390
<i>I got a bite?!</i>

06:52.720 --> 06:55.970
<i>I can hardly believe it!</i>

06:56.350 --> 06:58.410
<i>Wait, wait, wait. Don't be hasty!</i>

06:58.410 --> 07:02.810
<i>Would an affiliate of a secret society 
expose himself so carelessly?!</i>

07:03.080 --> 07:06.280
<i>Calm down! I'm being tested!</i>

07:12.680 --> 07:14.160
<i>I know. I'll stop.</i>

07:14.160 --> 07:17.290
<i>I can't pass anything more off as coincidence.</i>

07:17.960 --> 07:18.810
<i>But...</i>

07:19.480 --> 07:21.980
<i>there are some things I can't tolerate.</i>

07:22.580 --> 07:27.180
<i>Ignoring that incorrect 
emblem wouldn't feel right.</i>

07:28.240 --> 07:32.530
<i>Of course, I'd have to correct Solitaire 
himself to make a difference.</i>

07:32.530 --> 07:34.260
<b>Critical Hit!!</b>

07:34.260 --> 07:37.940
I... I see. I'll take that under advisement.

07:38.390 --> 07:40.330
Now, if you'll excuse me.

07:40.330 --> 07:42.110
Oh, one last thing.

07:42.790 --> 07:47.690
Do you know a girl with pigtails 
who uses a wheelchair?

07:49.360 --> 07:53.360
I can no longer understand 
what she is saying,

07:53.760 --> 07:57.830
but she appears distressed 
by the path you walk.

07:58.140 --> 08:01.680
<i>Her ghost is materializing 
the form of a wheelchair.</i>

08:02.030 --> 08:04.420
<i>She must have used it for a long time.</i>

08:05.230 --> 08:07.650
<i>And she doesn't seem capable 
of conversation anymore, so...</i>

08:08.180 --> 08:11.340
I suppose that must be my guardian spirit.

08:11.560 --> 08:15.250
If I remember anyone of that description, 
I'll be sure to face her.

08:20.040 --> 08:23.440
I'd better not force her to pass on, then.

08:23.440 --> 08:26.830
<i>You've got me intrigued, fortune teller.</i>

08:26.830 --> 08:31.570
<i>I thought he was a fraud, passing 
off hot reading as supernatural,</i>

08:31.570 --> 08:34.280
<i>but then, how would he know about </i>her<i>?</i>

08:34.930 --> 08:38.110
<i>What can he see?</i>

08:39.120 --> 08:43.330
That was <i>so cool</i>! And wasn't he hot?

08:43.330 --> 08:45.530
You only care about looks.

08:45.530 --> 08:47.570
Oh, is it starting to rain?

08:48.100 --> 08:51.210
Crap! I didn't bring an umbrella!

08:51.210 --> 08:54.010
You can borrow mine. I've got a raincoat.

08:54.010 --> 08:56.320
For real?! Thanks!

08:54.240 --> 08:57.230
<i>Water will damage my makeup.</i>

08:57.550 --> 09:01.270
<i>I wish I had half those girls' energy.</i>

09:03.110 --> 09:04.590
<i>I see.</i>

09:05.050 --> 09:09.480
<i>So, you've set your sights on the same place.</i>

09:12.460 --> 09:14.870
Still, what a weird coincidence.

09:15.570 --> 09:19.100
Two people in a row asked the same question.

09:20.420 --> 09:22.120
That said,

09:22.490 --> 09:27.660
that raincoat makes me question your taste.

09:22.490 --> 09:28.170
<b>Fire Safety</b>

09:34.030 --> 09:36.470
I have an update on the 
Solitaire investigation.

09:36.470 --> 09:41.930
We have 100 investigators on the streets, 
and we're checking surveillance cameras.

09:41.930 --> 09:44.720
We've left him with fewer places to go,

09:44.720 --> 09:50.860
but we still have no idea 
what he's trying to achieve.

09:51.460 --> 09:54.970
We know what's got his attention right now.

09:55.780 --> 09:57.280
<b><i>Ten'a Sorimura
self-professed
magician</i></b>

09:55.780 --> 09:57.280
<b><i>Youji Iwazono
(46)
Yougan-gumi
Leader</i></b>

09:55.780 --> 09:57.280
<b><i>The Poisoner
(60–70~)</i></b>

09:59.050 --> 10:00.550
Should we lure him out?

10:01.120 --> 10:05.540
Only a few people know there's 
an error in that symbol.

10:06.040 --> 10:10.880
But we can't point that out here, can we?

10:10.880 --> 10:14.840
No. The enemy could be anywhere.

10:15.130 --> 10:18.330
Whoever they are,
they drove Hosorogi-san into hiding.

10:18.840 --> 10:22.310
If we scatter bait carelessly, 
we'll be the ones who get eaten.

10:26.010 --> 10:29.850
I know hunting down Solitaire is my job,

10:30.220 --> 10:33.360
but having more than one goal 
throws off my instincts.

10:33.360 --> 10:37.320
If we catch Solitaire,
they'll make their move, too.

10:37.530 --> 10:41.280
We should just be glad that we have 
more officers at our disposal.

10:41.280 --> 10:45.740
You're sipping coffee while you 
make us work our asses off?

10:46.070 --> 10:50.210
For a guy whose career hit a dead end,
you sure act high and mighty.

10:50.530 --> 10:55.670
Thanks for the compliment. I've at least 
risen high enough to order you around.

10:56.880 --> 11:02.890
And if you've got the energy to gripe, 
you're not "working your asses off."

11:03.100 --> 11:04.810
Don't let this go to your head.

11:05.490 --> 11:09.810
Lots of guys still hold grudges from 
your time as Hosorogi's flunky.

11:10.050 --> 11:12.520
Oh, is that so?

11:13.230 --> 11:15.860
The only ones mad at me 
about Internal Affairs cases

11:15.860 --> 11:20.360
would be crooked cops who 
can't get away with it anymore.

11:20.710 --> 11:22.950
I'm telling you to know your place!

11:22.950 --> 11:27.620
You might be a big shot in your precinct, 
but you'd better watch it here.

11:29.210 --> 11:33.130
Are you too scared to hold any conversation
 you can't turn into a pissing contest?

11:33.130 --> 11:35.350
Is that your problem?

11:35.350 --> 11:38.590
Even internet trolls have better manners.

11:38.590 --> 11:40.050
Why, you—

11:42.630 --> 11:44.280
Now, now.

11:45.430 --> 11:46.410
You—

11:47.140 --> 11:49.600
H-Hey! Let g—

11:49.600 --> 11:52.310
Arase, I'm fine.

11:54.860 --> 11:55.730
Arase.

11:58.330 --> 12:00.810
I said I'm fine.

12:05.820 --> 12:11.370
How about we all agree to stop 
picking on the weak, then?

12:13.790 --> 12:15.500
Do you know where you stand, Arase?

12:16.200 --> 12:18.710
That sting operation of yours was illegal.

12:18.710 --> 12:21.450
What do you think'll happen to 
you if you make more trouble?

12:21.450 --> 12:24.160
If you like, we could always 
<i>make up</i> some trouble to—

12:24.160 --> 12:27.890
Don't be silly. I've already 
been punished for the sting.

12:28.120 --> 12:31.390
Tozawa-san really let me have for that, too.

12:31.390 --> 12:33.100
Oh, there you are.

12:33.100 --> 12:37.270
What are you wasting time picking 
fights here for, Iwa-san?

12:37.270 --> 12:38.720
Whoops! Close one.

12:39.230 --> 12:40.770
Are you okay?

12:40.770 --> 12:42.280
Y-Yeah.

12:42.590 --> 12:43.650
Huh?

12:45.620 --> 12:49.660
Well, now. Is this that trouble you 
were going to "make up"?

12:49.660 --> 12:51.380
Honestly.

12:51.380 --> 12:54.540
You used that fall to 
dislocate your <i>own</i> shoulder?

12:54.540 --> 12:59.360
You're lucky I was here. Arase-kun 
wouldn't know how to treat this.

13:00.430 --> 13:02.780
There. That's one problem solved.

13:02.480 --> 13:05.470
m 0 0 l 280 0 280 100 0 100

13:02.480 --> 13:05.470
<b>Shinjuku Precinct Community Safety Division
Assistant Head of Materials Compiling Group #3 

Danjo Tozawa</b>

13:05.680 --> 13:09.950
Man, what a relief. I'm so glad 
there wasn't any major trouble.

13:09.950 --> 13:12.390
m 0 0 l 340 0 340 100 0 100

13:09.950 --> 13:12.390
<b>Member of the same group
MPD Shinjuku Precinct Arrest Technique Tournament 
Individual Division Champion

 Ranmaru Yatsu</b>

13:12.390 --> 13:15.350
<b>I looked pretty cool
reining in Arase, right?</b>

13:12.390 --> 13:15.350
<b>They both saw me
do that, right?</b>

13:12.610 --> 13:14.670
Y-Yeah.

13:15.680 --> 13:17.060
What's going on here?!

13:17.550 --> 13:22.030
Why, Senior Commissioner 
Habaki. Nothing at all, sir.

13:22.540 --> 13:27.950
I just performed first aid on an 
injured colleague. Isn't that right?

13:28.650 --> 13:30.740
Y-Yes.

13:31.430 --> 13:33.790
W-We'll be on our way.

13:37.250 --> 13:39.460
So, what happened,

13:39.460 --> 13:40.650
Iwanome?

13:43.460 --> 13:45.380
I understand the situation.

13:45.680 --> 13:50.650
They may be in the wrong, 
but try not to provoke them, would you?

13:51.100 --> 13:55.250
Solitaire's video already has us all on edge.

13:55.250 --> 13:57.460
That stuff about a mole?

13:57.860 --> 14:03.230
Yes, although the brass seems to 
think he staged the shooting himself.

14:03.230 --> 14:10.190
Still, try not to make waves.
I can only cover for you so much.

14:10.500 --> 14:14.840
I'm grateful that you're willing 
to cover for me at all, sir.

14:15.410 --> 14:17.530
Now, if you'll excuse me.

14:19.510 --> 14:20.920
Be careful.

14:24.750 --> 14:26.120
This is still only a possibility,

14:26.120 --> 14:31.630
but more troublemakers could be mixed 
up in this case. Lemmings included.

14:31.630 --> 14:33.390
There's a scary thought.

14:34.020 --> 14:38.050
That's why I need all the 
trustworthy people I can get, Pop.

14:38.050 --> 14:38.850
Oh?

14:39.060 --> 14:44.320
I was <i>going</i> to ask you not to make things 
any worse between HQ and the precinct.

14:44.320 --> 14:48.390
Those guys just have it in for <i>you</i>, Iwa-san.

14:48.390 --> 14:50.030
Real funny, Yatsu.

14:50.480 --> 14:54.490
Well, either way, Comps-3's 
job doesn't change.

14:54.490 --> 14:58.040
We'll put our hearts and souls
 into seeing it through.

14:58.040 --> 14:59.610
Protecting this town

15:01.160 --> 15:02.970
from those troublemakers' crazy games.

15:08.920 --> 15:14.010
m 0 0 l 220 0 220 280 0 280

15:08.920 --> 15:14.010
<b>From: Big Sis

Dear Little Brother,
I couldn't trace Miyabi Hosorogi 
through finance, communication, 
relationships, or any other means.
 Oh, and there's a summer cold 
going around, so take good care 
of yourself. Curry goes bad 
sooner than you'd think,
 so make small batches and
 finish them. Whatever you do,
 don't make any mistakes
 with Young Miss Sayo.

Your ever-loving sister,
Imbi</b>

15:09.610 --> 15:14.010
I don't believe it. Not even the Lei 
intelligence network can find Hosorogi?

15:15.340 --> 15:16.840
Footsteps on the roof?

15:17.490 --> 15:18.400
Whew!

15:18.400 --> 15:22.520
No matter how often I do it,
landing on rooftops always gives me a thrill!

15:22.520 --> 15:25.820
Is it the guilty pleasure of knowing 
I'm about to commit a crime?

15:25.820 --> 15:30.550
The tension of knowing my 
enemies might be lying in wait?

15:30.550 --> 15:33.340
No! No, no, no!

15:33.340 --> 15:35.240
This is intoxication!

15:35.700 --> 15:40.710
And since the works of the great Edogawa 
Rampo are now in the public domain,

15:40.920 --> 15:46.460
perhaps no one will get mad if I call 
myself the Phantom With Twenty Faces?

15:47.090 --> 15:48.130
No, wait.

15:48.550 --> 15:51.310
Rampo's fans will still 
take umbrage, won't they?

15:51.110 --> 15:52.340
<b><i>And quite seriously,
 too...</i></b>

15:52.650 --> 15:54.300
What do you think?

15:57.470 --> 16:00.230
Well, this is certainly a warm reception.

16:00.230 --> 16:03.350
It seems my hunch was right on the money.

16:03.350 --> 16:05.760
Now, would you kindly tell me

16:05.760 --> 16:11.190
about the organization you belong to,
and about that symbol,

16:11.530 --> 16:13.880
Fortune-Telling Corpse God?

16:13.880 --> 16:16.530
Or should I say... Polka Shinoyama-kun?!

16:18.400 --> 16:21.750
Please don't lump me in with that weakling.

16:23.840 --> 16:24.810
<i>Who are you?!</i>

16:25.060 --> 16:26.500
m 0 0 l 80 0 80 130 0 130

16:25.060 --> 16:26.500
<b>Meanwhile, 
Polka is...</b>

16:42.330 --> 16:46.690
<i>Kagome kagome.</i>

16:47.120 --> 16:51.570
<i>The bird in the basket, locked away.</i>

16:51.780 --> 16:56.070
<i>When will it come out to play?</i>

16:56.340 --> 17:01.040
<i>At night before the break of day</i>

17:01.040 --> 17:05.290
<i>the crane and turtle slipped away.</i>

17:05.920 --> 17:09.990
<i>Who's that behind you?</i>

17:09.990 --> 17:12.740
Hurry! The pit swallowed the army!

17:12.740 --> 17:14.200
What about General Daryl?!

17:14.200 --> 17:16.760
The Home-wrecker Dragon took 
him and his whole force!

17:16.760 --> 17:19.850
They deserted?! I told him 
dragons couldn't be trusted!

17:20.080 --> 17:21.870
Where are the prince and empress?!

17:20.970 --> 17:23.850
What are you doing, fool of an apprentice?

17:21.870 --> 17:23.850
I can't contact the imperial guard.

17:24.230 --> 17:27.010
I placed wards to shield us from notice.

17:24.470 --> 17:26.440
Has an annexed principality revolted?!

17:26.440 --> 17:28.700
No, nothing human could cause that!

17:27.010 --> 17:31.070
Otherwise, they'd be dragging us 
to the front lines as we speak.

17:31.640 --> 17:33.240
Won't I go, you ask?

17:34.440 --> 17:37.510
I've no taste for joining in the 
fools' self-inflicted downfall.

17:38.460 --> 17:42.660
I left all our acquaintances I 
could reach in Romelka's care.

17:45.140 --> 17:48.860
Utsurojuza spoke the truth. The time is ripe.

17:49.430 --> 17:51.290
You should get ready, too.

17:52.620 --> 17:54.350
Ready for what, you ask?

17:54.970 --> 17:59.720
For living free, off the empire's leash.

18:00.600 --> 18:05.260
Honestly, I had you possess 
an older skeleton,

18:05.260 --> 18:08.140
but mentally, you were 
a child to the very end.

18:09.090 --> 18:13.570
Oh, well. I suppose you'll grow up eventually.

18:14.860 --> 18:17.690
We have unlimited time.

18:18.190 --> 18:24.710
But by the same token,
you'd better treasure those who don't.

18:26.470 --> 18:28.750
Oh, forgive me.

18:28.750 --> 18:30.460
Forgive me, Teacher.

18:31.870 --> 18:34.000
I failed.

18:34.900 --> 18:36.510
I couldn't protect them.

18:37.080 --> 18:38.760
I couldn't save them.

18:39.580 --> 18:41.720
I couldn't even forgive.

18:42.650 --> 18:45.780
I've tarnished the powers you taught me.

18:46.260 --> 18:49.140
And I'm ashamed to face 
anyone from the empire.

18:49.500 --> 18:53.860
<b>I became an enemy</b>

18:49.500 --> 18:53.860
<b>of the world.</b>

18:49.930 --> 18:53.040
I became an enemy of the world.

18:54.890 --> 18:57.960
I fled from the world.

18:59.450 --> 19:03.280
I no longer felt affection for any—

19:05.400 --> 19:08.870
You're as dimwitted as ever, my dear friend.

19:09.540 --> 19:11.690
Your... Majesty...

19:14.190 --> 19:15.800
<b><i>FWAP</i></b>

19:14.480 --> 19:15.800
<b><i>FWAP</i></b>

19:14.770 --> 19:15.800
<b><i>FWAP</i></b>

19:15.060 --> 19:15.800
<b><i>FWAP</i></b>

19:15.310 --> 19:15.800
<b><i>FWAP</i></b>

19:15.610 --> 19:15.800
<b><i>FWAP</i></b>

19:16.060 --> 19:18.320
C-Cut it out! I'm awake!

19:21.040 --> 19:22.640
I smell something burning...

19:25.320 --> 19:29.520
<b>This world is a buggy program</b>

19:26.580 --> 19:29.520
<b>Are you a termite?</b>

19:26.580 --> 19:29.520
<b>Or are you a bird eating the bug?</b>

19:30.700 --> 19:31.810
What's this?

19:33.290 --> 19:35.840
What, <i>now</i> you're afraid of ghosts?

19:36.290 --> 19:39.910
No, if a ghost was behind this, I would know.

19:41.390 --> 19:42.810
It's still hot.

19:46.600 --> 19:47.410
<b>Incoming Call</b>

19:46.600 --> 19:47.410
<b>Number
Withheld</b>

19:47.410 --> 19:48.870
<b>Incoming Call</b>

19:50.330 --> 19:51.370
Hello?

19:51.370 --> 19:55.340
Is this Polka Shinoyama?

19:51.370 --> 19:55.340
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

19:55.660 --> 19:56.880
Who is this?

19:59.410 --> 20:00.550
Hello?

20:00.550 --> 20:02.920
Are you also

20:00.550 --> 20:03.510
<b>Number Withheld</b>

20:03.880 --> 20:07.130
<i>a Bastard Child of Sabaramond?</i>

20:09.390 --> 20:10.610
How...?

20:09.390 --> 20:14.670
<b>Speaking</b>

20:09.390 --> 20:14.670
<b>Number
Withheld</b>

20:11.590 --> 20:14.170
How do you know that name?

20:17.190 --> 20:19.740
I see. So that's how it is.

20:20.190 --> 20:22.870
Really, they're so inconsiderate!

20:22.870 --> 20:26.740
Forcing me to play along with 
a quirk of fate like this!

20:27.000 --> 20:29.910
<i>"They"? Who does he mean?</i>

20:30.270 --> 20:34.250
<i>Isn't he the wanted criminal 
everyone's talking about?</i>

20:34.250 --> 20:37.720
<i>No reaction?! Who is that boy?!</i>

20:37.720 --> 20:40.960
<i>I said that like I know what's 
going on, but I'm winging this!</i>

20:40.960 --> 20:42.420
<i>Think, Solitaire!</i>

20:42.920 --> 20:46.230
Well, whatever. Once I catch you,

20:46.660 --> 20:49.470
I can take my time with the interrogation.

20:51.010 --> 20:53.480
Don't be hasty, lad.

20:53.480 --> 20:57.480
You're still still young,
and it's 3:00 in the morning.

20:57.480 --> 20:59.310
So go to bed like a good little—

21:00.070 --> 21:02.190
I'm 19.

21:04.950 --> 21:05.940
<i>He's fast!</i>

21:06.970 --> 21:09.370
I'll admit, no child moves like that.

21:09.680 --> 21:11.910
But you're not so fast that I can't—

21:19.330 --> 21:20.590
Excuse... me?

21:32.660 --> 21:34.560
So, there's been activity.

21:34.560 --> 21:38.520
But not quite the sort I was expecting.

21:39.860 --> 21:42.010
I can't believe that thrill-seeker

21:42.530 --> 21:46.030
is fighting one of my 
grandfather's bodyguards.

21:47.740 --> 21:49.570
We'll make our move, as well.

21:51.780 --> 21:55.920
When it comes to securing a conflict zone,

21:57.030 --> 21:59.360
the most important question

22:00.170 --> 22:02.750
is how to walk off with the spoils.
